    {
      "code": "upgrade_source_version_ladder",
      "status": "fixed",
      "detail": "the deleted-raw summary table was listed as a v1.14.6 marker although every 1.14.x release creates it, so a real source of the pinned release was reported newer than the pin and refused with upgrade_source_version_unsupported: no real 1.x install could pass preflight",
      "file": "apps/manager-server/internal/service/upgrade/schema.go:366",
      "regression": "apps/manager-server/internal/service/upgrade/preflight_test.go TestSourceVersionAcceptsThePinnedReleaseSchema"
    },
    {
      "code": "upgrade_copy_in_interrupted_migration",
      "status": "fixed",
      "detail": "a copy-in killed after materialize and before the operation row committed left its provenance marker, but the resume compared the migration-rewritten database sidecars with the backup, deleted the marker and then refused to replace the members it had already moved, so the window the marker exists for could not be resumed",
      "file": "apps/manager-server/internal/service/upgrade/copyin.go:657",
      "regression": "apps/manager-server/internal/service/upgrade/copyin_test.go TestCopyInResumesAfterAnInterruptionInsideTheMigration"
    },
    {
      "code": "upgrade_wizard_unreachable_after_copy_in",
      "status": "fixed",
      "detail": "an unfinished operation admits only the fixed Bootstrap surface, and the copy-in target replaces usage.sqlite so it carries no Fresh record for the canonical continuation: both wizard read routes answered 404 while the wizard had a stage recorded, so the operator could never see the copy_in or reconcile the process had just written. The two reads are now mounted beside the Upgrade entry leaf on the fixed surface, under the same gate and the same source credential, and retire with completion",
      "file": "apps/manager-server/cmd/cpa-manager-plus/startup_discovery.go:73",
      "regression": "apps/manager-server/cmd/cpa-manager-plus/startup_upgrade_wizard_test.go TestStartupServesTheUpgradeWizardFromTheCopiedOperation"
    },
    {
      "code": "upgrade_wizard_unreachable_on_a_refused_mount",
      "status": "fixed",
      "detail": "the mount lookup counted a mount's usage.sqlite with os.Stat, which follows a symbolic link: the mount looked like a source, the credential read then refused the linked file under the shared database file policy, and the entry page and both wizard reads answered 503, so the operator could not reach the page that names the condition. The mount question now asks the credential read's own inspection through one MountDatabase lookup, so a mount the policy refuses holds no database for the surface: the credential resolves to the Manager store, the surface stays reachable, and status and preflight report upgrade_source_symlinked for that mount",
      "file": "apps/manager-server/internal/service/upgrade/preflight.go:397",
      "regression": "apps/manager-server/cmd/cpa-manager-plus/startup_upgrade_surface_test.go TestStartupUpgradeSurfaceAcceptsOneCredentialEverywhere"
    },
    {
      "code": "upgrade_source_version_pinned",
      "severity": "blocker-for-u1-1b",
      "detail": "the contract accepts v1.14.4, so a real v1.14.10 source is refused with upgrade_source_version_unsupported; the U1-1b re-pin is what makes the planned fixture usable",
      "file": "apps/manager-server/internal/domain/bootstrap/contract.go:12",
